What Tars uses from Von
  - Von's model class (von.models.option_marker.OptionMarkerModel), its training
    collator and loss (training/train_option_marker.py) and its synthetic
    general-reasoning generator (training/generate_synthetic_decisions.py).
    These are imported from a Von checkout at run time, not copied.
  - Von 1.2's weights are the starting point of every Tars fine-tune.
  - pipeline/train.py and tars/model.py adapt parts of Von's training loop and
    model loading; each file's header says which parts.

What Tars changed or added
  - Three decision questions for commands, built from a skill catalog:
    split (does a new step start here?), route (which family?) and skill
    (which skill in that family?) (tars/questions.py).
  - A planner that chains the three questions into steps (tars/planner.py)
    and an HTTP server (tars/server.py).
  - A full fine-tuning pipeline: label generation, dataset build with speech
    recognition noise and general-reasoning replay, time-budgeted training on
    Apple GPUs or CUDA, and a promote/keep evaluation (pipeline/).
  - A macOS app for defining a catalog, collecting labels from your own AI
    provider or any MCP client, reviewing them, training and comparing models (app/).

Training labels
  Tars's own training phrasings were written by an LLM (Anthropic's Claude,
  through the Claude Code CLI). Labels you make with the app come from
  whatever provider you choose. Check your provider's terms before
  redistributing generated datasets.
